Foundation-model configs no longer accept settings that did nothing. Removed: `QuantizationConfig` and the `quantization` and `input_kind` fields of `NeuralFineTuneConfig` (QLoRA quantizes with fixed settings when `train_mode="qlora"`); `DeviceConfig.precision` (training always ran in float32); `CheckpointConfig.save` and `monitor` (every value saved the weights at the end of training, so a checkpoint is now written whenever `output_dir` is set, as before); and the `train_mode`, `n_outputs` and `normalize_embeddings` fields of `FoundationEmbeddingModelConfig` (a frozen backbone never trains, has no head, and never normalised its embeddings). `model_key` is required in both foundation-model configs instead of defaulting to a model that does not exist. A frozen backbone gets a `device` setting (`FoundationEmbeddingModelConfig.device`): it had none and always ran on the automatically chosen device.
